<section class="business-section" id="signals">
  <div class="business-wrap">
    <div class="business-section-head">
      <div>
        <span class="business-eyebrow">When founders call</span>
        <h2>Three sentences I hear on the first call.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="business-section-intro">None of them are about a specific bug. They're about a system that stopped being legible — usually right after it started working.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="business-signals">
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">The roadmap slipped twice and nobody can tell me why.</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Usually it isn't velocity. It's that no one owns the sequence, and every estimate is a negotiation. I make the sequence explicit and the owner singular.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">We have eight engineers and no one owns the architecture.</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Eight people making locally reasonable choices produce a system nobody can reason about. I write the decisions down as ADRs so the reasoning survives the next hire — and my exit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">We're raising, and the technical story falls apart in the room.</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Investors don't need your stack. They need to hear that scaling is a spending decision, not a rewrite. I help you find out whether that's true, then say it plainly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
